1. Categories of Request Reasons in Consignment Replenishment WIO

Even though exact values depend on configuration, in real implementation they fall into these standard groups:

A. Standard Replenishment Reasons (Core PAR Flow)

These are the most common ones you will ALWAYS see.

1. Fill Up
Normal replenishment to restore PAR
Triggered when stock drops due to usage

👉 Flow:

PAR check applies
Usually no special approval if within PAR
2. Consumption Based Replenishment
Based on actual usage trend
Reflects increased clinical consumption

👉 Flow:

Often leads to Over PAR evaluation
May trigger One-Time approval
3. PAR Restoration
System-driven or planned refill to bring stock back to target level
Sometimes same as Fill Up but used for analytics separation
B. Demand-Driven Reasons
4. Forecast Demand
Planned future usage (not current consumption)
Used for upcoming surgeries or monthly planning

👉 Flow:

Can trigger PAR exceed scenario
Approval depends on deviation
5. Buffer Stock Increase
Customer wants higher safety stock than PAR

👉 Flow:

Almost always triggers Permanent Approval
May require Demand Planner approval
C. Event-Based Reasons
6. Workshop / Training Support
Stock required for training, demos, workshops

👉 Flow:

Temporary increase
Often STC-heavy usage
One-Time approval common
7. Surgical Case Support
Specific patient / surgery requirement
Highly time-bound requirement

👉 Flow:

Priority approval routing
May bypass normal threshold logic in some configs
D. Exception / Urgent Reasons
8. Emergency Replenishment
Critical stock shortage situation

👉 Flow:

Fast-track approval
May trigger red alert immediately
Higher priority than PAR logic
9. Rush / Expedited Requirement
Delivery urgency rather than stock logic
Linked with logistics constraints

👉 Flow:

Often tied with Non-Standard Delivery approval (AF rules)
E. Controlled / Restricted Reasons
10. Limited Release Product Request
Restricted products (mapped via ZS10 table)

👉 Flow:

Strict validation
Cannot mix with normal products
Account-specific availability only
11. New Product Introduction (NPI)
Product launch / trial placement

👉 Flow:

Controlled distribution
Often restricted to selected hospitals
F. Master Data / System Reasons
12. PAR Adjustment Request (Z23)
NOT a replenishment reason
Used to change PAR value itself

👉 Flow:

Goes to Demand Planner
Impacts master data, not just order
